  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday)\nIssued at 122 AM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nLong-term forecast impacts: Gradual warm-up, with rain chances \nreturning by the end of the week.\n\nDiscussion: Shortwave ridging returns briefly to the Plains on \nTuesday. This will help clear the mechanism from the cold/wet/cloudy \npattern. With southwest flow building over the northern Plains \nduring the day, winds here will shift southerly and potentially get \nrather breezy. All of this suggests dry and slightly warmer weather.\n\nThat southwest mid-level flow will dominate more of the Plains by \nWednesday. Breezy conditions and warmer temperatures are likely to \nfollow each of Wednesday and Thursday with more substantial moisture \nreturn occurring by day 3 or 4 of the return flow regime. With a \nfavorable upper-air pattern and increasing moisture, storm chances \nwill increase on Thursday/Friday, though a specific window or \nlocation for those storms has yet to emerge on ensemble data.\n\nMeister",
